# for (const line of lines) { const c = JSON.parse(line); c[0] === "p" ? .. : .. }
# Behind a test for Double storage `c[0] === "p"` is false by the type of the element. The read and the comparison go, and what is left names neither the list nor the guard.
# In storage for any value the list may hold the text, so that code answers for no such list. Nothing in the copy would show it, so the copy is refused where it is made.
# The same holds for the guard of another list, for a guard that proves something else or that comes over two edges, and for a value of a wider type than the value that it stands for.
